🔹 REST Security & ACID
REST does not have built-in security or ACID properties,
but we can implement them using:
JWT (JSON Web Token)
OAuth
HTTPS
Database transactions

📌 REST is Resource-Oriented
In REST, everything is a resource.
In REST, we use one resource and perform different operations using HTTP methods.
️ Same resource
✔️ Different HTTP methods
This is REST design.
Example: School Application
Resources:
Teachers
Students
Base URL:
/api/teachers
/api/students


🔹 What is Representational State Transfer?
Representational State Transfer means:
Data stored in the database is converted into a representation (JSON/XML)
That representation is transferred from server to client
Example:
GET /api/teachers/1
This means:
Fetch teacher data with ID = 1
Convert database state into JSON/XML
Send it as a response

🔹 SOAP vs REST URL Style
SOAP (Action-based):
saveTeacher,getTeacher,updateTeacher
REST (Resource-based):
/api/teachers


📌 REST Architectural Constraints (6)
If an API follows these constraints, it is called a RESTful API.

1️⃣ Client–Server Architecture
Client and server are independent
Server sends data in JSON/XML
Client decides how to display it (web, mobile, desktop)

2️⃣ Stateless
Server should not store client data
Every request is independent
Client must send all required information (token, headers, params)
Example:
HDFC Net Banking
Mobile app and web app both send credentials every time
👉 Even if the same client sends multiple requests, the server treats them as new requests.

3️⃣ Cacheable
Client can store responses in HTTP cache
Reduces repeated requests
Improves performance
Example:
Product list
User profile data

4️⃣ Uniform Interface
Same API works for:
Web app
Mobile app
Desktop app
Request structure remains the same
✔️ Consistency
✔️ Simplicity

5️⃣ Layered System
Application is divided into layers
Security layer
Business layer
Database layer
If one layer fails, others are not affected
✔️ Better security
✔️ Easy maintenance

5️⃣ Resorce oriented
—----------------------------------------
6️⃣ Code on Demand (Optional)
Server can send executable code to the client
Client can run that code if needed
✔️ Optional
✔️ Rarely used
Advantages of using REST API’s : 
Simple and Easy to Use
Lightweight and Fast because for XML processing it takes time 
Stateless Architecture Each request is independent, and the server does not store client state.
Separation of Client and Server (not monolithic arch) Frontend and backend can be developed independently Changes in UI do not affect backend APIs
Cacheable Responses Reduced server load
Supports Multiple Data Formats (JSON,XML,plain text)

